    "name": "Introduction",
    "section": 0,
    "summary": "<p id=\"yui_3_18_1_1_1789136813116_41\">Reality is intrinsically different from any of its models, giving rise to uncertainty. When tackling real-world problems, managing this uncertainty becomes essential. This course provides powerful tools for engineers and others who need to model complex phenomena using Artificial Intelligence techniques. Key application areas include (big) data analysis, classification, automatic control, robotics, the modeling of artificial and natural phenomena, user and device behavior modeling, decision support, and forecasting.<br><br>The course rigorously covers the theoretical foundations of various modeling approaches, highlighting their practical applications through comparisons of models, examples, and case studies. Additionally, it introduces design techniques for AI systems that incorporate these technologies.<br><br>This course replaces the long-standing Soft Computing course, maintaining its core focus on uncertainty while shifting some previously covered topics, now central to the Machine Learning, Neural Networks, Deep Learning, and Data Mining courses. In \"Uncertainty in Artificial Intelligence,\" we delve deeper into methods and approaches specifically designed to address the intrinsic uncertainty found in real-world applications.</p>\r\n<p id=\"yui_3_18_1_1_1789136813116_40\">Goals for this course are listed in the following.</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Presentation of the main issues in modeling the real world, including the possible sources of uncertainty and how it is possible to reduce their effect or cope with them.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Presentation  of basic knowledge about some technologies used to model uncertainty namely: Uncertainty measures, Logic-based approaches, Fuzzy Systems, Possibility systems, and Probabilistic Graphical Models (e.g., Bayesian Networks and Hidden Markov Models).</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Presentation of tools to implement the mentioned technologies.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Analysis of paradigmatic case studies to understand the applicability issues of the mentioned technologies.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Development of the ability to analyze a problem, to select the appropriate technology for a problem, to design data, architectures, and processes including the mentioned technologies</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Development of the ability to learn autonomously both declarative and procedural knowledge (thanks to innovative teaching methods, such as flipped class, and blended learning).</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<div>\r\n<p><strong>Expected teaching results</strong></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<ul id=\"yui_3_18_1_1_1756967394328_788\">\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Acquisition of basic knowledge about some technologies to treat uncertainty in AI systems, namely: Uncertainty measures, Fuzzy Systems, Possibility systems, and Probabilistic Graphical Models (e.g., Bayesian Networks and Hidden Markov Models).</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Acquisition of the ability to analyze a problem, to select the appropriate technology for a problem, to design data, architectures and processes for the mentioned technologies.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Acquisition of basic operational abilities to implement the mentioned technologies.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>Acquisition of the ability to present both the knowledge, the process, and the proposed solutions, as well as to analyze results and data</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li id=\"yui_3_18_1_1_1756967394328_787\">\r\n<p id=\"yui_3_18_1_1_1756967394328_786\">Acquisition of the ability to learn autonomously both declarative and procedural knowledge.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>",
    "summaryformat": 1,
    "uservisible": true,
    "visible": 1
  },
